  "notes": [
    "Regular -AR verb — follows standard endings in every tense, no exceptions.",
    "Often used with \"de\" + noun: *disfrutar de las vacaciones* (\"to enjoy the vacation\"), though it's also common without \"de\" before a direct object: *disfrutar la comida*.",
    "*Espero que disfrutes tu viaje.* (\"I hope you enjoy your trip.\")",
    "*Disfrutamos mucho de la fiesta anoche.* (\"We really enjoyed the party last night.\")",
    "Related: *el disfrute* (enjoyment, noun), *disfrutable* (enjoyable, adjective, less common), *pasarlo bien* (synonym phrase, \"to have a good time\")."
  ],
